## Preserve exactly

- Layout and visual hierarchy (hero, KPIs, search/filters, gallery cards, empty/error/loading states, create/detail/archive/lightbox flow)
- Crystal/glass surfaces, colors, glows, typography, icons, spacing, and animations
- Existing Gallery functionality, API calls, upload behavior, permissions, routes, and data behavior
- Gallery-related tests and their assertions

## Other work must stay independent

Work on Login, Dashboard, Clients, Bookings, Calendar, Invoice, and other modules without touching the files above.

If you must change shared CSS, layout shells, or shared files that Gallery *calls* (`ClientSearchSelect`, `clients-service`, `bookings-service`, `api-error`, `cn`):

- Do not alter `.dhara-gallery`, `.dhara-gal-*`, or `gallery-page.css`.
- Scope new styles so they cannot override Gallery descendants.
- Prefer new class names over changing globals used by Gallery.
- Other modules may *call* those shared files, but must preserve Gallery’s current appearance and functionality exactly. Do not edit the locked Gallery files listed above without explicit Gallery approval.

## Allowed exception

Only modify the Gallery module when the user clearly asks for a specific Gallery change in that conversation.

Do not weaken `.cursor/rules/locked-login-page.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/locked-dashboard.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/locked-clients-module.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/locked-calendar-module.mdc`, or `.cursor/rules/locked-invoice-module.mdc`.
